Negative control for the Code pane keeping up with the state (AC3.3 · D1).

Freezes the fence. The live criteria model is read ONCE, at setup, and the
computed then returns that snapshot forever — so the first paint is still
exactly right (the narrowing and the ordering on screen are the ones in the
call) and every later facet change leaves the snippet standing on stale state.

This is the whole distinction AC3.3 draws: the snippet is a COMPUTED over the
same criteria the filter bar writes, not a render-time sample of it. A pane that
only has to be right once passes every "carries exactly those options" case
while failing the one claim that makes Code a page feature rather than a
screenshot.

Nothing else moves — the serialisation, the copy path, the markdown fence and
the pruning rules are untouched — so a red here is the reactivity and not a
crash or a formatting drift.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: code-pane.spec.ts — the case that changes a facet on a mounted pane and
expects the fence to follow (and any case asserting the copied text follows a
later facet change). The first-render cases stay GREEN under the mutant, by
construction; if they go red too, the control has been over-applied.

  FOR THE PROVER: authored by the developer seat, which knew the line to mutate;
  it carries no verification run. Apply it blind, confirm the reactivity case
  goes red and the first-render cases stay green, then revert.

